// [nonadreno] bc-astc-gpu (port-common/modules/bc-astc-gpu; FN-60 / FN-61): GPU-decoded BC1 / BC2 / BC3 / BC7 stored as ASTC 4x4 LDR.
// Included by xbg_game.cpp inside its anonymous namespace, right after namespace bcgpu (it uses bcgpu's scratch buffers, BcJob, BcUpload,
// Image, recording_slot, Arena).
//
// Without device BC the GPU decode path (TEX-01, BcUpload + bcgpu) stores BC as RGBA8: 4x the memory and sampling bandwidth of BC3 /
// BC7, 8x of BC1. With this module a BC1 / BC2 / BC3 / BC7 texture that takes that path is created as VK_FORMAT_ASTC_4x4_UNORM / _SRGB
// (the BC format's sRGB-ness) and every batch BcUpload sends (whole uploads, partial / dirty-GOB uploads, CopyBufferToTexture of a
// GPU-written image) runs one more compute dispatch after the decoder: xbg_bc_astc_encode.comp reads the decoder's RGBA8 output and
// writes one 16-byte ASTC block per BC block into astc_buf (block g of the batch at 16 * g: tight rows per region), which is then copied
// into the image instead of the RGBA8 output. BC 4x4 blocks and ASTC 4x4 blocks cover the same texels, so every rectangle the engine
// uploads (whole levels, row bands, GOB blocks, block-aligned copies) is a whole-block rectangle of the ASTC image too.
//
// Decision (Image::bc_astc, at image creation, never changed later): per family (a BC format and its sRGB partner: views and copies stay
// inside one, xbg_bc_view_compatible), so two decoded images of one family that may be copied into each other have the same format:
//   DM_GFX_BC_ASTC (boot): auto (default) = on wherever the GPU decode path runs, except on Qualcomm (vendor 0x5143), where that path only
//   runs simulated (DM_GFX_SIM_GPU / DM_GFX_NATIVE_BC=0); 1 = force, also there; 0 = off: the old RGBA8 path, byte for byte;
//   GPU decode in use (bc_mode 2); this encoder built and passed its self-test (below); ASTC 4x4 UNORM and sRGB with SAMPLED,
//   SAMPLED_IMAGE_FILTER_LINEAR, TRANSFER_SRC and TRANSFER_DST in optimal tiling; both decode pipelines of the family passed their own
//   self-test (bcgpu::pipeline, DM_GFX_BC_SELFTEST). Then per image (xbg_bc_astc.h xbg_bc_astc_shape): single-sampled, not storage
//   (NVN flag 0x4: no ASTC storage views) and not linear (0x10: uploaded through the CPU-decoding single-buffer path), and the ASTC
//   overlay's keep rules (not 2D, VT-cache shape, BC3 arrays; DM_GFX_BC_ASTC_VT=1 lifts the last two), and the image format properties
//   of that shape. A texture that fails a per-image rule stays RGBA8 ("kept"); copies between it and an ASTC one of its family are
//   skipped and logged (copy_route).
//
// Every path that writes into a decoded image, for an ASTC one: whole upload (upload_banded -> BcUpload, GPU mode only), partial upload
// (partial_upload -> BcUpload), CopyBufferToTexture (guest_texture_write first, as before; a GPU-written image goes through
// copy_from_buffer -> BcUpload instead of the CPU decode), copy_texture (same-format ASTC blocks or skipped, copy_route), clear_texture
// (skipped and logged: vkCmdClearColorImage has no compressed formats), mutable upgrade (vkCmdCopyImage of the same format: fine),
// DM_GFX_BC_VERIFY (its image readback compares RGBA8 texels: ASTC batches are not attached), BcUpload's "no GPU pipeline" CPU fallback
// (cannot happen: the family's pipelines exist before an ASTC image does; a fatal error if it ever did), DM_GFX_ASTC_CPU substitutes
// and the single-buffer CPU decode (never ASTC: subst_cpu / linear excluded).
//
// Self-test (FN-61; once, at the first decoded BC texture of the process): the set of xbg_bc_astc.h xbg_bc_astc_kat (285 blocks:
// gradients, flat, alpha edges, GameNative's self-test block; random BC1 / BC1A / BC2 / BC3 / BC7 blocks of every mode decoded by the
// CPU decoder, BC2 / BC3 half with one alpha value so the direct path runs) encoded on this GPU through the real descriptor set, decoded on
// the CPU with xbg_astc_ref_decode.h: no error block, no all-zero block (an all-zero read is invalidated and re-read, then the test is
// submitted once more: GameNative's stale-read retry) and every block's MSE <= the host's * 1.25 + 10 (xbg_bc_astc_kat.h, generated by
// engine/tests/bc_astc_encode_test). Failure: the encoder is off for the process, every image stays RGBA8 (the old path).
// Log: "NVN BC astc: self-test ... -> gpu|off". Other lines: "NVN BC astc: DM_GFX_BC_ASTC=...", "NVN BC astc: <family> -> ...",
// "NVN BC astc: kept RGBA8 ...", "NVN BC astc: images=...", "NVN BC astc: copy skipped ...", "NVN BC astc: clear ... skipped".
//
// Reuse without an image (a pre-build pass over the game's texture files, a cache writer): stage an XbgBcGpuBatch, make_job(batch input in a
// staging buffer, NVN format) and record it with bcgpu::record into any command buffer: input copied into bcgpu::in_buf, decoded, encoded;
// the ASTC blocks of block g are at astc_buf + 16 * g when the dispatch has finished (take them with a sink, below, or a copy of your own).
//
// [hook] sink (default off: null, no consumer in this module): set bcastc::sink and every ASTC batch also copies its blocks into the
// recording slot's readback arena right after the encode; when the slot retires (its fence signalled, on the translation thread) the sink
// gets (user, texture serial, NVN format, the batch's copy regions = level / layer / texel rectangle + offset of its blocks, the blocks).
// Meant for a disk cache (DOS2's lazy cache, D3 / TL2 packs) to take a fast first entry that a CPU astcenc result can replace later;
// see port-common/migration/bc-astc-gpu.md for the cost (readback bandwidth, hashing, writing) and the keys.
// Tree shims (D16 defaults; a tree without the record thread / drvc / pt_mode defines these before the include: migration/bc-astc-gpu.md).
#ifndef XBG_BCA_CMD
#define XBG_BCA_CMD(f) vkrec::Cmd##f                       // command recording (D16: through vkrec; others: vkCmd##f)
#endif
#ifndef XBG_BCA_SYNC
#define XBG_BCA_SYNC() vkrec::sync(vkrec::W_FINISH)        // before a direct queue submission (D16); others: nothing
#endif
#ifndef XBG_BCA_SUBMIT
#define XBG_BCA_SUBMIT(si,fence) (pt_mode?(dm_present_queue_lock(),xbg_bca_submit_locked(si,fence)):vkQueueSubmit(cfg.queue,1,&(si),(fence)))
static inline VkResult xbg_bca_submit_locked(const VkSubmitInfo &si,VkFence f){const VkResult r=vkQueueSubmit(cfg.queue,1,&si,f);dm_present_queue_unlock();return r;}
#endif
#ifndef XBG_BCA_MODULE_LOCK
#define XBG_BCA_MODULE_LOCK drvc::Lock compile(true);      // D16 compile lock; TL2 / DOS2: gpguard::ModuleLock serial;
#endif
#ifndef XBG_BCA_PIPE_LOCK
#define XBG_BCA_PIPE_LOCK gpguard::Lock serial;
